 Venture Capital Deals 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 🚑 Ausperbio , an SF-based biotech focused on chronic hepatitis B, raised $120m in Series C funding. RA Capital Management led, joined by insiders HanKang Capital, Qiming Venture Partners, YuanBio Venture Capital, and CDH Investments. axios.link/4cl8w7N 

 🚑 EIT Pharma , a Kirkland, Wash.-based biotech focused on infectious diseases, raised $35m in Series A funding. Propel Bio Partners led, joined by Good Ventures and Arrowtown. axios.link/4x1aFwZ 

 • S-Transistors , a Finnish quantum tech startup, raised €2.6m in pre-seed funding led by Lifeline Ventures . axios.link/4qMwRJK 

 • TrustedRouter , an AI routing startup, raised $1.25m from individuals like Sam Lessin, Bill Tai, and Linda Avey. axios.link/45YX8Le 

 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 Private Equity Deals 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 • Bernhard Capital Partners acquired Revenew International , a Houston-based provider of cost recovery and performance improvement solutions, from Sentinel Capital Partners . axios.link/45UbxbJ 

 • EQT and Allianz each are weighing £5b takeover bids for AA , a U.K. roadside assistance firm, per Sky News. AA owners are TowerBrook Capital Partners , Warburg Pincus , and Stonepeak . axios.link/4wY6uC0 

 ⚡ Toesca agreed to buy a 64% stake in Chilean water utility Suralis from Algonquin Power &amp; Utilities (NYSE: AQN) for $126.5m upfront. axios.link/4cDmCSj 

 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 Public Offerings 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 No U.S. IPOs are scheduled for this week. 

 • Bamboo Insurance Services , a Midvale, Utah-based homeowners insurer backed by CVC Capital Partners and White Mountains , filed for an IPO. It reports $14m of net income on $173m in revenue for the first half of 2026, and plans to list on the NYSE (BMB). axios.link/4xuiUTb 

 🚑 Electra Therapeutics , an SF-based biotech focused on immunology and cancer, filed for an IPO. It plans to list on the Nasdaq (ETRA) and has raised $300m from OrbiMed (9% pre-IPO stake), Westlake BioPartners (7.1%), Redmile (7.1%), Aventus (6.2%), EQT LSP (6.2%), and New Leaf Ventures (4.4%). axios.link/4xuiSux 

 • Graf Acquisition II , an industrials SPAC led by James Graf, refiled for a $220m IPO. axios.link/4zKTvWT 

 • Longsys , a Shenzhen-listed memory chip maker, plans to raise up to $801m in a Hong Kong float. axios.link/4gDjpTM 

 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 Liquidity Events 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 ⚡ Apollo and Triton agreed to sell Kelvion , a German provider of thermal management and heat exchange tech, to SLB (NYSE: SLB) for $3.4b in cash (plus assumption of $700m in debt). axios.link/3V4EhMo 

 🚑 Astorg and Montagu Private Equity are seeking to sell Nemera , a French maker of delivery devices for GLP-1s that could fetch around €3b, per Bloomberg. axios.link/3T1Fofm 

 🚑 Eli Lilly (NYSE: LLY) agreed to acquire Merida Biosciences , a Cambridge, Mass.-based biotech focused on serious autoimmune and allergic diseases, for up to $2.88b in cash. Merida had raised $154m from Third Rock Ventures, Bain Capital Life Sciences, BVF Partners, GV, and Perceptive Advisors. axios.link/4i43mkq 

 ⚡ Oneok (NYSE: OKE) agreed to pay $4.43b for Permian Midland Basin natural gas gathering ‌and processing assets from Brazos Midstream , backed by Old Ironsides Energy and EnCap Flatrock Midstream . axios.link/4cnA24G 

 
 
